# AI Platform

The gateway and the shared tracing backends are installed, and model access is a catalog item.

## The gateway

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **URL** | ${litellm_url} |
| **Admin console** | ${litellm_console_url} |
| **OpenAI-compatible base URL** | `${litellm_api_base}` |
| **Namespace** | `${litellm_namespace}` |
| **Model aliases offered** | ${model_aliases} |

The master key is the root credential of the gateway and is deliberately not shown here, because
every building block output is stored in cleartext. It lives in the Secret `${master_key_secret}` in
the namespace `${litellm_namespace}`.

**The admin console holds at most five users.** Native single sign-on is free in the open-source
proxy up to that number, and the sixth login locks out everyone. Plan the platform team's console
access around it.

## Shared backends

| Backend | Where |
|---------|-------|
| Postgres, for virtual keys, teams, budgets and spend | database `${postgres_database}` on the shared PostgreSQL Flex instance |
| ClickHouse, for every tenant's traces | `${clickhouse_host}` |
| Valkey, for every tenant's ingestion queue | `${valkey_host}` |
| Object storage, one bucket per tenant | created per tenant, in the STACKIT project of this architecture |

Each tenant's tracing instance is published under `${apps_domain}`, on a hostname derived from the
workspace and the project.

## Self-service

The gateway is registered as the meshStack platform **${platform_identifier}**. Every landing zone
below makes model access mandatory, so a project that lands in one receives its team, its virtual
key, its tracing instance and the Kubernetes Secret carrying the credential without ordering
anything.

| Landing zone | Allowed models | Budget |
|--------------|----------------|--------|
%{ for lz in landing_zones ~}
| ${lz.display_name} (`${lz.name}`) | ${lz.models} | ${lz.max_budget} per ${lz.budget_duration} |
%{ endfor ~}

Publish the landing zones you want application teams to see, and they can start ordering projects
on them.
